  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are largely weakened on incident reporting and customer disclosure: S1 only covers serious incidents, and S5 makes the 8/100k threshold a notification/assessment trigger rather than a mandatory recall, with an open-ended corrective-action alternative. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% review threshold but no automatic sales stop, and exempts existing models, strongly favoring Northwind. S3 and S4 are within acceptable ranges (6-year retrofit, 36-month suppression), satisfying both red lines while giving each side timing concessions."
